<#job/observed-writer-state> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/raf/report/1#specRef> "docs/interfaces.md: store counters (store format); docs/architecture.md section 7." .
<#job/observed-writer-state> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/raf/report/1#summary> "Durability, pressure and table rewrite state stay writer-local and may be held across commits; a mutable borrow publishes a small Observe::View copy when it ends, and status reads only that copy, so status never waits for a pressure pass, rewrite step or commit. Read-lease handle counts come from each registry's ledger, mirrored on every registry change and locked only to copy rows, so status never waits for a registry a listing holds while it waits for the writer." .
