<#job/source-context-timeline-cache> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/raf/report/1#summary> "One derived source timeline is maintained atomically with authoritative record/time publication; an open resets it with one range deletion only when its generation marker shows it stale, and the source-context online migration rebuilds it through the shared bounded catalog pager. Every source-local reader walks the one timeline, source_context::Timeline::walk, over the database under the writer or a snapshot, which reads the cache once it is complete and the authoritative primary time index, filtered to the source, until then; there is no second reader or separate fallback." .
