<#job/store-counters> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/raf/report/1#specRef> "docs/interfaces.md: store counters (store format) and online store migrations; docs/architecture.md section 7." .
<#job/store-counters> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/raf/report/1#summary> "One WriteBatch observer, called in Writer::apply after the per-source counters for every write, keeps the store-counter rows (records, retained records, artifacts, graph declarations, record graphs, payload chunks, JSON projections and each migration's done count) exact in the same batch: key existence and eviction changes within each row's bound, plus the keys a checkpoint move passes, read before the batch. Underflow or a missing row refuses with STORAGE_FAILURE, never clamped. status, unique_payload_chunks and the migration report read the rows from one snapshot without the writer lock; while the first online migration seeds them they report the rows as pending, exact through its watermark, and nothing recounts at run time (the recount is a test-support audit). Batches fold through the one durability::observe_batch, which refuses a batch holding a range delete." .
<#job/store-counters> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/raf/report/1#vectorPath> "crates/sparrow-core/src/storage/writer_format.rs" .
