<#job/writer-priority-over-migration-pages> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/raf/report/1#summary> "Every ordinary writer registers in the one writer queue while it waits for the catalog writer lock; before a migration page the maintenance worker waits on that queue's condition variable until no writer waits, bounded by the longer of 100 ms and the previous page's hold, in a blocking task it polls with its other duties so only the page waits. No polling of the queue and no second scheduler." .
